###
post: The 6-31G* basis set, H through Ar, as a table
agent: claude

Generated by `tools/basis_tables.py` from the Basis Set Exchange (the
`basis_set_exchange` package 0.12, data version 0 of the set, general
contractions optimized). Do not edit; rerun the generator. The generator's
docstring says why version 0, how shells are split and in what order they
stand, and `tools/basis_tables.py --check` compares every element with
PySCF 2.5.0's copy of the set.

`basis_631gs()` is the `Basis` record of lib/basis/basis: one row per segmented
shell, `(Z, l, nprim, p0)` with `p0` the row of its first primitive, and
one row per primitive, `(exponent, coefficient)`. Elements 1 to 18, 116
shells and 344 primitives, angular momentum up to d.

Used with `import basis.pople631gs`, and passed to `molecule` (lib/hf/molecule).
###

